  "youtube": {
    "title": "Why One Bad Moment Ruins Your Whole Day #shorts",
    "description": "Six great hours, five bad minutes, and you remember it as the worst day ever? That's the peak-end rule.\n\nYour memory doesn't average an experience. It mostly keeps the most intense moment and the ending. In a classic experiment, most people chose to repeat a LONGER painful ice-water trial over a shorter one, because the longer one ended a little gentler.\n\nSo protect your endings: end hangouts, study sessions and days on a good note, and fix a bad ending when you can.\n\nResearch: Kahneman, Fredrickson, Schreiber & Redelmeier (1993), \"When More Pain Is Preferred to Less\", Psychological Science.\n\n#shorts #psychology #peakendrule #friendship #mindset #animation #selfimprovement",
